            <div xml:id="d516">

                <pb facs="0767" n="653" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg653"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.4A6/235: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-03-17T18:00:00-05:00">March 17, 1931—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>31. Department’s telegram, July 22, 1930.<anchor n="89" xml:id="d516-f1"/> Inform
                    the Secretary General of the League of Nations, in reply to his note of June 14,
                        1930,<anchor n="89" xml:id="d516-f2"/> that this Government accepts the
                    invitation to participate in the conference on the limitation of the manufacture
                    of narcotic drugs to be held on May 27, 1931, and that the delegates will be
                    John K. Caldwell, Chairman; Harry J. Anslinger (Commissioner of Narcotics); Dr.
                    Walter Lewis Treadway (Assistant Surgeon General, Chief, Division of Mental
                    Hygiene); and Sanborn Young, a member of the Senate of the State of
                    California.</p>
                <p>The Department desires that Winthrop Greene<anchor n="90" xml:id="d516-f3"/> act
                    as Secretary and Vice Consul Smith<anchor n="91" xml:id="d516-f4"/> act as
                    disbursing officer of the delegation. Names of technical and clerical assistants
                    will be communicated later.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
